WEBVTT
NOTE
Demo subtitle track for the AniZora sample catalogue.
Original placeholder text, written to exercise the player's subtitle pipeline:
track selection, styling, positioning and the Off switch.

STYLE
::cue {
  background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);
}

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
This is the English demo subtitle track.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.000
If you can read this, WebVTT parsing and rendering are working.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The intro marker ends around here — try the Skip Intro button.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Open the settings menu to change subtitle size, colour and background.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Switch quality from the same menu. Playback position is preserved.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
A mid-roll ad cue point sits at 45 seconds when video ads are enabled.

7
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Switch audio to English Dub — the tone changes from 440Hz to 660Hz.

8
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Try seeking. The burnt-in timer should match the scrub bar exactly.

9
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Keyboard shortcuts: space, arrows, F, M, P, and number keys 0-9.

10
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:26.000
The outro marker begins at 78 seconds — Skip Outro appears there.

11
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
End of the demo track.
